Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Change Manager Job id: 160005. Salary: £45,031 - £51,174 per annum, including London weighting allowance. Posted: 06 October 2026. Closing date: 25 October 2026. Business unit: Transformation Office. Department: Transformation Office. Contact details: Minal Khambalikar.  minal.khambalikar@kcl.ac.uk Location: Lavington Street. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us: The Transformation Office sits at the heart of King's College London, supporting senior leaders to turn strategy into action and deliver meaningful, lasting change across the University. As part of the Transformation Office, the Change Management team plays a critical role in helping King's successfully navigate and embed change. We work across some of the University's most significant strategic initiatives, partnering with leaders, colleagues and stakeholders to ensure change is delivered in a way that engages people, builds capability and achieves sustainable outcomes. Joining our team offers the opportunity to contribute to transformation that impacts staff, students and the wider King's community while developing your expertise within a supportive and collaborative environment. About the role: We are seeking an enthusiastic and proactive Change Manager to join our growing Change Management team within the Transformation Office. This is an exciting opportunity to play a key role in delivering some of King's most important transformation programmes. Working closely with the Senior Change Manager, you will help shape and deliver change strategies that support successful adoption, increase engagement and build organisational readiness for change across the University. The role offers significant variety and exposure, providing the opportunity to work with senior leaders, academic colleagues, professional services teams and external partners. You will be responsible for developing and delivering change management activities that help people understand, engage with and embrace change. You will support the creation and delivery of change management plans, including stakeholder engagement, impact assessments, sponsor roadmaps, communications activities and approaches to managing resistance. Alongside programme delivery, you will coach and support sponsors and leaders through the change journey, helping to build confidence and capability across the organisation. As part of King's wider ambition to strengthen change capability, you will also contribute to the development of the University's Change Community of Practice and Transformation Network. You will help deliver training, coaching, tools and practical guidance that empower colleagues to lead and deliver change successfully. This role would suit someone with strong stakeholder engagement skills, a collaborative approach and a genuine passion for helping people navigate change. In return, you will have the opportunity to work on high-profile initiatives, develop your professional expertise and make a meaningful contribution to the future of King's. This is a full-time position (35 hours per week) offered on a fixed-term basis until July 2028. We operate a hybrid working model, with colleagues typically spending two days per week on campus and three days working remotely. About you: To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Educated to Degree Level standard or equivalent relevant experience Knowledge and understanding of change management methodologies, tools and techniques. Prosci is our chosen methodology. Experience as a change manager on transformation projects or equivalent relevant project delivery environment Strong stakeholder management skills, including the ability to build “trusted advisor” relationships with senior colleagues. Strong interpersonal skills and teamwork, tact, diplomacy and perseverance Experience in planning and facilitating training and awareness/engagement events. Desirable criteria Experience within the Higher Education sector or adjacent/similar sector and understanding of the context we operate in A Prosci / equivalent change management qualification Experience in change communications Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit’ pages. Interview date to be confirmed Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Change Manager | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/160005-change-manager Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
