in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Answers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Electrical Engineer - Guy's Job id: 153245. Salary: £39,076 per annum inclusive of London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 20 July 2026. Closing date: 18 October 2026. Business unit: Estates & Facilities. Department: Engineering - Guy's. Contact details: Paul Imber.  Paul.imber@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guys Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us: At King’s College London, our Engineering Team plays a critical role in ensuring our facilities are safe, efficient and well maintained to ensure our vibrant community is able to learn, innovate and shape the future. We’re looking for a skilled and dedicated Electrical Engineer to join our team. About the role: The Electrical Engineer will be responsible for delivering a high-quality electrical maintenance service across the University. This includes carrying out both reactive and planned preventive maintenance (PPM), ensuring statutory compliance, identifying and resolving faults, and supporting the ongoing development of the maintenance function through training and real-time reporting systems. The role will ensure completion of all mandated Health & Safety training, including eLearning modules, within required timeframes to maintain compliance with statutory and organisational standards. Carry out planned preventive maintenance (PPM) to ensure the reliability, safety, and efficiency of electrical systems, installations, and equipment. Respond promptly to reactive maintenance requests and resolve faults efficiently to minimise disruption to university operations. Perform inspection, testing, and maintenance of electrical systems to ensure statutory and legal compliance (e.g. emergency lighting, fixed wire testing, PAT testing). Diagnose and repair electrical faults across a wide range of systems, including distribution boards, lighting, small power, and control panels. Assist with installation and modification of electrical equipment and systems as required. Ensure all works are completed in accordance with relevant legislation, regulations, and university safety procedures. Maintain up-to-date records of all statutory testing, maintenance, and repairs using the university’s CAFM (Computer-Aided Facilities Management) app. Participate in audits and compliance reviews as needed. Accurately document work carried out in real time using digital reporting tools or mobile devices. Communicate effectively with contractors and team members to coordinate maintenance activities. Provide feedback on recurring issues or inefficiencies to help improve service delivery and system performance. Undertake ongoing technical training and statutory certification to maintain up-to-date knowledge of best practices and legal requirements. Attend toolbox talks, health & safety briefings, and compliance training sessions. To undertake training and qualify as Authorised/Responsible/Competent Persons as required. Support apprentices or junior engineers with knowledge-sharing and mentorship where appropriate. Form part of the dedicated-on call engineering team with scheduled / rota on call weeks. Required to be available for seven days to take calls, attend site when required to investigate and deal with reported issues. Unresolved issues need to be escalated to duty manager as and when required. In addition to working in a dynamic environment, King’s College London offers many benefits including: A comprehensive range of technical training and personal development to help you thrive and progress A generous annual leave allowance to support a healthy work-life balance Competitive pension schemes plus access to exclusive discounts on shopping etc A wide range of health and wellbeing benefits This is a full time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an indefinite contract About you: To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Recognised electrical qualification (e.g. NVQ Level 3, City & Guilds / AM2/ Electrical Apprenticeship JTL or similar) 18th Edition IET Wiring Regulations certification Proven experience in a similar maintenance role, ideally within a large and complex estate IT literate - Use of iPad / SharePoint / Emails / MS Teams / CAFM reporting Strong fault-finding skills and ability to work independently under pressure Good knowledge of health and safety practices in a maintenance environment Good knowledge and understanding of building services systems and safe working practices (inclusive of mechanical systems) Desirable criteria Experience working in an educational or public sector environment HV/LV Authorised Person Level 3 Award in Periodic Inspection and Testing of Electrical Installations 2391/2394+2395 Knowledge of energy efficiency or sustainability initiatives related to electrical systems Mechanical qualification or relevant experience / BMS / Controls knowledge and experience Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit’ pages. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics par