      "description": "King’s Prize Fellowship | King's College London Skip to main content Study Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Study Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Undergraduate Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate taught Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate Research Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional Education Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Education & Languages Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Study Abroad Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Foundation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Summer and Winter Programmes Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Accommodation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Mobility Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Visit King's Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding opportunities Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Student Services Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Academic Calendar Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Sport Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Libraries & Collections Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Answers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link King’s Prize Fellowship Job id: 154845. Salary: £53,947 - £63,350 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 07 August 2026. Closing date: 26 October 2026. Business unit: Research Management & Innovation. Department: Research Strategy & Development. Contact details: Kate Smith.  Healthresearchdevelopment@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us King’s College London invites applications for the prestigious King’s Prize Fellowships, supporting exceptional postdoctoral scientists ready to launch independent research careers. Fellowships provide a competitive salary and up to £30,000 in research expenses for 18–24 months, enabling fellows to establish a distinctive research programme and prepare competitive applications for intermediate level fellowships from major funders. Fellowships may be held in any part of King’s College London, but both the project and the fellow’s career objectives must be primarily focused on biomedical or health-related research. Due to the competitive nature of this fellowship and the focus on targeting intermediate level fellowships, we normally advise applicants to have a minimum of three years postdoctoral experience. Before applying for this fellowship, you must have the agreement of a permanent academic member of staff to act as your sponsor, in a department with a strong rationale for hosting the fellowship. The sponsor must have appropriate experience to provide strong research and career development mentorship. About the role To be successful in this role the applicant will need to be able to show a body of research outputs and the level of thought leadership and development towards independence required to be competitive as a future research leader. To secure a fellowship you will need to design a research plan that is clearly aligned to a future intermediate fellowship application, providing a strong platform for future success. During the fellowship you will be expected to design and conduct a range of experiments in relation to your research plan and prepare and present findings of research activity to colleagues for review purposes. The applicant will draft and submit research papers to appropriate peer reviewed journals and prepare and submit intermediate research fellowships applications, to schemes supporting a career stage and providing a level of funding adequate to support successful transition towards a permanent research leadership position. The applicant will contribute to the overall activities of the research team and department as required and hold responsibility for ensuring equipment is maintained in working order and assist with laboratory upkeep. The applicant is to always comply with the requirements of the Health and Safety regulations with responsibility for the health, safety and welfare of others in the working environment and ensure confidentiality on all matters and information obtained during the course of their employment. The above list of responsibilities may not be exhaustive, and the post holder will be required to undertake such tasks and responsibilities as may reasonably be expected within the scope and grading of the post. This is a full time post and you will be offered an a fixed term contract of up to 24 months. Research staff at King’s are entitled to at least 10 days per year (pro-rata) for professional development. This entitlement, from the Concordat to Support the Career Development of Researchers , applies to Postdocs, Research Assistants, Research and Teaching Technicians, Teaching Fellows and AEP equivalent up to and including grade 7. Visit the Centre for Research Staff Development for more information. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience. If you have applied for the King’s Prize Fellowship previously, please note that we will accept no more than one re-application. If you choose to reapply you should set out clearly how your application has changed. Essential criteria 1.      Higher degree (MD, PhD or equivalent) in a relevant subject area: must have submitted PhD thesis before taking up the post 2.      Demonstration of understanding of, and commitment to, an academic career 3.      Evidence of team working skills 4.      Demonstration of the potential for scientific independence and the ability to lead a research team 5.      Significant publications in peer reviewed journals 6.      Potential to become a leader in your chosen field Desirable criteria 1.      Prizes or distinctions 2.      Postdoctoral research experience in an internationally renowned laboratory (we would normally expect at least 3 years postdoctoral experience). Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information on what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Submitting your application To apply you must prepare a research and career plan in the form of a grant application. Please ensure that you download a copy of the application form that you must use to submit your fellowship proposal. The form includes guidance. Your application will be reviewed by academic referees, and shortlisted candidates will be invited to present their research plans at an academic selection panel. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. We hope to hold interviews in the week commencing 1st February 2027. Confirmation will be provided to shortlisted candidates. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box King’s Prize Fellowship | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/154845-kings-prize-fellowship Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
