to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni King's College London Job id: 160346 . Salary: £53,947 - £63,350 per annum inclusive of Lon . Posted: 12 October 2026 . Closing date: 01 November 2026 . Business unit: King's Business School . Department: Strategy, Intl Mgt & Entrepreneurship . Contact details: Professor Johann Fortwengel . johann.fortwengel@kcl.ac.uk Location: Strand Campus . Category: Academic & Teaching . Back to job search About us: King's Business School, King's College London, seeks to appoint a Lecturer in Management to join the Department of Strategy, International Management & Entrepreneurship (SIME). SIME advances rigorous and impactful research on questions that matter to business and society, including how firms formulate and implement strategy, navigate geopolitical uncertainty, compete across borders, respond to technological and institutional change, and lead transitions towards more productive, sustainable and responsible ways of operating. Our interdisciplinary community brings together expertise in strategy, international management, innovation, sustainability, responsible business and geopolitics. Colleagues publish in leading journals, secure competitive research funding, and engage with partners in industry, government and civil society. SIME contributes to core undergraduate teaching in Strategic Management, International Business, and Business Ethics and Sustainability. The Department also hosts the FT-ranked MSc in International Management and contributes specialist teaching across King's Business School. Located in central London, King's offers an internationally connected environment for developing ambitious research, research-informed education and engagement with organisations, policymakers and wider society. About the role: We seek an outstanding scholar in Management who will contribute to the Department's research and education across a broad range of management questions. We welcome applications from candidates whose research addresses important organisational, managerial, technological, or societal challenges. Relevant areas may include organisation and management theory, organisational change, work and employment, leadership, decision-making, business and society, corporate responsibility, sustainability, resilience, supply chains, and other areas that complement the Department's existing strengths. This list is indicative rather than restrictive, and we particularly welcome candidates with a clear, ambitious, and distinctive research agenda. The postholder will develop an internationally visible programme of research, publish in leading journals, seek external research funding, and build productive collaborations within SIME, across King's, and with national and international partners. They will contribute high-quality, research-informed teaching across relevant undergraduate and postgraduate programmes and, where appropriate, supervise doctoral researchers. We seek a collegial academic who will contribute actively to the intellectual life and citizenship of the Department and School. This appointment forms part of the Department's continued investment in research excellence, educational quality, and international visibility. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an indefinite contract. About You: To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria A PhD in Management or a closely related discipline, awarded or submitted by the start date. A clear, coherent and ambitious programme of independent research in management or a related field. Evidence of the ability to produce high-quality research and publications of originality, significance and rigour, commensurate with career stage (as evidenced by publications or the potential to publish in elite journals). Evidence of high-quality, research-informed teaching and assessment, or clear potential to achieve this, at undergraduate and/or postgraduate level. Ability to contribute flexibly to management teaching and to the development and delivery of modules across relevant undergraduate and postgraduate programmes. Evidence of effective communication, organisation and collaborative working. Commitment to academic citizenship and to an inclusive and collegial academic community. Potential to build productive research collaborations within and beyond the Department. Desirable criteria Evidence of publications in elite peer-reviewed journals. Evidence of grant applications, or clear potential to attract external research funding. Experience of module design, module leadership or curriculum development. Experience of supervising dissertations, doctoral researchers or other student research. Evidence of research impact or engagement with organisations, policymakers, professional communities or civil society. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information on what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit’ pages. Apply now Apply now Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link"
    },
