 Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Project Manager Job id: 160245. Salary: £45,031 to £52,514 per annum including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 12 October 2026. Closing date: 01 November 2026. Business unit: King's Digital. Department: King's Digital Production. Contact details: Philippa Keyworth.  Philippa.keyworth@kcl.ac.uk Location: Waterloo Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us Our mission is to provide transformative, high-quality digital education, so students can learn, wherever they are. We collaborate with academics and professional services staff across the university, and with our external partners, to design, develop and deliver a wide range of educational programmes. Our learners study with us from across the world, choosing when and where they study, working around their schedules. We are a dynamic team with ambitious growth targets in a priority area of development for King’s. We proudly foster a supportive culture and community which prioritises both individual and collective wellbeing. As part of hybrid working at King’s, all team members can work remotely for part of the week if they wish. About the role The Project Manager is responsible for the production management and coordination of online and blended modules and programmes. Working with a diverse team made up of developers, designers, and media producers, you will lead project teams to ensure that the content produced is delivered to agreed schedules, within resource allocations, and meets our quality standards. You will forge strong relationships with your project teams, our wider directorate, stakeholders in faculties and with partners external to King's, which will include providing excellent reporting and maintaining clear and timely communication throughout the duration of each project. This role will project management both the production of existing module updates and the design and build of new modules. You will be responsible for the delivery of the production, from the start of the development process to its completion and delivery to students. You will ensure your project team(s) communicate effectively and have the required resources to perform at a high level. You will proactively problem-solve, mitigate risks, and escalate to seniors when necessary. This is a full time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an a fixed term contract until November 2027. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Experienced in project management practices and tools. Experience in collaboration and co-ordination of tasks across teams. Knowledge of digital production processes. Excellent relationship management and communication skills. Skilled user of project management software e.g. MS Excel, ClickUp and able to learn and adapt to using new software quickly. Ability to create clear timelines, timeboxes, project documentation and report on risks and issues. Ability to use initiative and proactive problem-solving to adhere to delivery dates, with attention to detail and a commitment to quality. Ability to manage conflict, solve problems and create a positive working environment. Desirable criteria Educated to degree level. Knowledge of Traditional and Agile project management methodologies. Experienced user of Microsoft Office, Google Products and communication tools. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. This is a fixed term maternity cover post. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Project Manager | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/160245-project-manager Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
