 key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni King's College London Job id: 160365 . Salary: £65,091 - £74,613 per annum inclusive of London Weighting Allowance . Posted: 12 October 2026 . Closing date: 01 November 2026 . Business unit: King's Business School . Department: Strategy, Intl Mgt & Entrepreneurship . Contact details: Professor Johann Fortwengel . johann.fortwengel@kcl.ac.uk Location: Strand Campus . Category: Academic & Teaching . Back to job search About us: King's Business School, King's College London, seeks to appoint a Senior Lecturer in Strategy to join the Department of Strategy, International Management & Entrepreneurship (SIME). SIME advances rigorous and impactful research on questions that matter to business and society, including how firms formulate and implement strategy, navigate geopolitical uncertainty, compete across borders, respond to technological and institutional change, and lead transitions towards more productive, sustainable and responsible ways of operating. Our interdisciplinary community brings together expertise in strategy, international management, innovation, sustainability, responsible business and geopolitics. Colleagues publish in leading journals, secure competitive research funding, and engage with partners in industry, government and civil society. SIME contributes to core undergraduate teaching in Strategic Management, International Business, and Business Ethics and Sustainability. The Department also hosts the FT-ranked MSc in International Management and contributes specialist teaching across King's Business School. Located in central London, King's offers an internationally connected environment for developing ambitious research, research-informed education and engagement with organisations, policymakers and wider society. About the role: We seek an outstanding scholar whose research advances major themes in strategy, with a particular focus on technology and innovation. The successful applicant will complement and strengthen SIME's established capabilities in strategy, international management, innovation, sustainability, responsible business and geopolitics. We welcome theoretically ambitious and methodologically rigorous research across strategy. Of particular interest is work examining how technology and innovation shape firm strategy, competitive advantage, corporate scope, global supply chains, business models, organisational capabilities, industry evolution, ecosystems, platforms, and relationships among firms, markets and institutions. Relevant work may also address artificial intelligence and emerging technologies, digital transformation, international strategy, non-market strategy, or the strategic implications of industrial, technology and innovation policy. We particularly welcome research that connects these questions to geopolitical change, geoeconomic fragmentation or business-government relations, while remaining open to different theoretical traditions, levels of analysis and methodological approaches within strategy. The postholder will develop an internationally excellent and visible research programme, publish work of originality, significance and rigour, pursue external research funding, and build productive collaborations within SIME, across King's and internationally. They will deliver high-quality, research-informed teaching, including core strategy and relevant specialist subjects, contribute to doctoral supervision, and undertake academic leadership and citizenship appropriate to Senior Lecturer level. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week) offered on an indefinite contract. About You: To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria A PhD in Strategy, Management, Innovation, International Business or a closely related discipline. An established and coherent programme of independent research that advances major themes in strategy, with a particular focus on technology and innovation. A strong record of high-quality publications in elite peer-reviewed journals, commensurate with career stage. A track record of developing competitive research proposals and, where appropriate, securing external research funding, individually or collaboratively. A strong record of high-quality, research-informed teaching and assessment, including the ability to contribute to core strategy teaching at undergraduate and postgraduate levels. Experience of successfully supervising doctoral researchers, or substantial experience of doctoral supervision appropriate to career stage. Evidence of academic leadership and substantial contribution to academic citizenship, alongside effective and collegial collaborative working. Ability to build and sustain productive national and international research collaborations. Desirable criteria Research that connects strategy, technology and innovation with geopolitics, international strategy, non-market strategy, business-government relations, industrial policy or institutional change. Experience of leading externally funded research projects or collaborative research programmes. Evidence of research impact or sustained engagement with business, government, policymakers or civil society. Experience of programme, module or curriculum leadership and development. Experience of mentoring early-career researchers, editorial activity, or leadership and service within relevant scholarly associations. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information on what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit’ pages. Apply now Apply now Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link"
