 to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Senior Research Operations Engineer Job id: 158826. Salary: £45,031 - £52,514 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 18 September 2026. Closing date: 18 October 2026. Business unit: Research Management & Innovation. Department: Advanced Research Computing. Contact details: Shane Warren.  shane.warren@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us e-Research (soon to be known as Advanced Research Computing) at King's College London is expanding with the mission to help enable and facilitate computational and data-intensive research across KCL Faculties. We regularly add to our HPC cluster and Cloud infrastructure, making our environment highly heterogeneous. This means we get to work with a range of hardware, including the latest GPUs (e.g., B200, RTX 6000 Blackwell Pro, H200) and CPU architectures that, even if they increase complexity, generate the kinds of problems we love! This role in our Operations Team provides support for the day-to-day running of the infrastructure and services provided by e-Research, as well as specialist assistance across the academic and research lifecycle across the full spectrum of faculties at King's. Details of the infrastructure and services provided by e-Research are available on https://docs.er.kcl.ac.uk Early applications are encouraged, as we reserve the right to close the advert early if a high volume of suitable applications is received. About the role We encourage attendance to at least two conferences a year and personal development with an allocation of 10% of time dedicated to working on projects or activities that support professional development in a relevant field. We are particularly looking for applicants who appreciate and can solve complex problems and are ready to step into technical leadership and shape culture. Experience deploying AI models for practical or specific research purposes and familiarity with concepts such as RAG and MCP is also highly valued. We also expect the capacity, with mentorship from senior members of the department, to be able to develop high-quality technical consultancy skills translating research requirements into costed funding proposals. For an informal chat, or any specific questions about the role, please contact stuart.morrison@kcl.ac.uk About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Post graduate degree with significant computational / computer science components or demonstrable equivalent experience in relevant technologies Strong verbal and written communication skills Experience with advanced operations in a production Linux environment such as scripting (e.g. bash, awk), configuration management (e.g. Puppet, Ansible), scientific packaging frameworks (e.g. Spack, Easybuild) Competence in a high-level programming language (e.g. Python, Golang) and demonstrable experience in at least one relevant technology (e.g. HPC, Cloud computing, storage hardware configuration) Experience using AI assisted software development (e.g. VSCode CoPilot, Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, OpenCode) Ability to facilitate development of and provide guidance for more junior staff and colleagues. Strong customer service ethos (able to cater for technical novices to subject matter experts) Desirable criteria Significant Python development skills (e.g. working with YAML and JSON for significant ETL operations) Significant web development skills (e.g. using frameworks such as Laravel, serving sites from docker containers) Configuring and diagnosing issues with computer networks (in a production environment) Configuring and diagnosing issues with Linux based storage systems (in a production environment) Significant Linux administration experience (in a production environment) Experience in deploying open weights AI models locally with frameworks such as LiteLLM, Olama and familiarity with concepts such as RAG and MCP. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. Interviews are due to be held in October. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Senior Research Operations Engineer | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/158826-senior-research-operations-engineer Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
