ation Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link SPRE Project Manager Job id: 160486. Salary: £53,947 - £63,350 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 12 October 2026. Closing date: 25 October 2026. Business unit: Research Management & Innovation. Department: Research Performance. Contact details: Ceri Margerison.  ceri.margerison@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us We require a highly organised individual with strong project management, communication and negotiation skills to join the REF, KEF and Research Impact team within the Research Management & Innovation Directorate as ‘SPRE Project Manager’. About the role The post holder will be responsible for overseeing the development of all aspects of the Strategy, People and Research Environment (SPRE) element of King’s submission to the 2029 Research Excellence Framework (REF): the Institution Level Statement (ILS) at university level and the Unit Level Statements (ULS) for each of the 26 REF Units of Assessment (UoAs) to which King’s submits. They will liaise with academic and Professional Services staff across King’s faculties – including UoA Leads, Research Culture teams and research support staff - to manage the coordination and drafting of the Unit Level Statements, ensuring synergy between these and the ILS. They will support the identification and gathering of data to feed into the quantitative elements of the submission, and will be the central contact point for advice and guidance on the SPRE element of REF. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week), offered on a fixed term contract until 31 July 2029. This is a hybrid role, with an expectation of attendance on campus a minimum of five days a month, and additional days according to business need. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria 1.      A degree, or substantial vocational and relevant management experience demonstrating project management ability. 2.      Detailed knowledge and understanding of the Research Excellence Framework (REF) assessment process, and of REF guidance and policy, including the requirements of the Strategy, People and Research Environment (SPRE) component. 3.      A proven track-record of excellent organisation and project management, with experience of managing processes and delivering through and with others. 4.      Experience in developing and implementing innovative strategies and plans. Ability to problem solve, making complex decisions with significant organisational impact. 5.      Excellent written, verbal and interpersonal communication skills including the ability to negotiate, influence and motivate academic and Professional Services staff, at all levels of seniority. 6.      Experience of building effective collaborative relationships across the organisation and working successfully with diverse groups of stakeholders. 7.      Proven analytical and research skills, ability to analyse and interpret complex data. Desirable criteria 1.      Experience using and developing Power BI dashboards. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. The interview date is to be confirmed. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation 