Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Student Email Manager Job id: 159945. Salary: £43,031-£52,514 per annum including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 06 October 2026. Closing date: 27 October 2026. Business unit: Global Student Recruitment & Admissions. Department: Student Marketing & Communications. Contact details: Karan Nathan.  karan.nathan@kcl.ac.uk Location: . Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search About us King's College London is one of the world's leading universities, with a global reputation for excellence in education, research and societal impact. Located in the heart of London, King's is home to over 40,000 students and 10,000 staff from across the world and is consistently ranked amongst the UK's and world's leading universities. About the role We are looking for a Student Email Manager to lead the planning, delivery and optimisation of email communications across the student recruitment journey. Working within the Student Marketing & Communications team, you will manage email campaigns that support prospective students from enquiry through to enrolment, ensuring communications are timely, engaging and data-driven. You will lead the development of email marketing activity, manage campaign delivery, provide guidance to email officers, and use insight and performance data to continuously improve engagement and conversion. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an indefinite term contract. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Educated to degree level and/or with substantial relevant experience in email marketing and campaign management. Proficiency in email marketing tool Microsoft Dynamics and experience using CRM platforms and customer journeys or marketing automation. Strong collaboration and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build, maintain and manage stakeholder relationships. Ability to analyse and interpret data, make informed recommendations, produce reports and monitor progress. Strong project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. Ability to create engaging and visually appealing email content. Excellent written and verbal communication and presentation skills. Working knowledge of data protection requirements for email marketing. Desirable criteria Experience of email marketing in higher education or student recruitment. Experience in line management, providing guidance, support and development, and fostering a collaborative, high-performing team environment. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. The Student Email Manager is a business-critical role within the Student Marketing Funnel team, responsible for delivering and optimising email communications throughout the student recruitment journey. Email remains one of King's most effective channels for engaging prospective students, nurturing applications, supporting offer holder conversion, and driving enrolment. The role manages strategic email planning, audience segmentation, automated journeys, campaign delivery, testing and performance analysis across multiple recruitment cycles. Its work directly supports student recruitment targets by increasing engagement, application conversion and enrolment rates through timely and personalised communications. The role also ensures compliance with data protection, consent management and communication governance requirements, reducing operational and reputational risk. Working closely with Recruitment, Admissions, Faculties and Digital teams, the post improves efficiency through automation and scalable communications, allowing large volumes of prospective students to receive personalised content without significant manual intervention. Without this role, the university would face reduced capacity to deliver recruitment communications at scale, impacting conversion activity, student experience and recruitment performance. The position supports income generation through improved student recruitment outcomes and protects the university's investment in CRM and marketing technology. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Student Email Manager | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/159945-student-email-manager Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
