o return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Student Web & Comms Manager - INTERNAL ONLY Job id: 159925. Salary: £43,031-£52,514 per annum including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 07 October 2026. Closing date: 18 October 2026. Business unit: Global Student Recruitment & Admissions. Department: Student Marketing & Communications. Contact details: Olivia Pembroke.  olivia.pembroke@kcl.ac.uk Location: Waterloo Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search THIS VACANCY IS OPEN TO INTERNAL CANDIDATES ONLY About us The Student Website & Communications team is part of Student Marketing & Communications within Global Student Recruitment & Admissions at King’s College London. We develop and deliver high-quality content and communications that support the University’s student recruitment, conversion and enrolment objectives. Working across the Directorate and wider University, we help ensure student-facing content is accurate, audience-focused, impactful and aligned with institutional priorities. About the role We are looking for a Student Web & Communications Manager to lead the planning, development, delivery and continual improvement of student-facing content and messaging at King’s. The role has particular responsibility for student recruitment web content and acts as a Lead Content Editor for Global Student Recruitment & Admissions.    You will provide specialist expertise in web content management, copywriting, content design, search engine optimisation, generative engine optimisation, accessibility, web standards and enterprise content management systems. Working closely with Digital Content, Digital Solutions, faculties, external agencies and specialist suppliers, you will act as a primary point of contact for student recruitment web content. You will help improve web templates, content structures and user journeys, contribute to web development through Scaled Agile delivery and planning, and ensure content is consistently governed and optimised. You will also support the development and implementation of the University’s student recruitment messaging and Student Value Proposition. The role leads brand-level content and communications projects across formats including websites, external profile sites, print guides, presentations, email funnels and other student-facing communications, while collaborating with the teams that own our email, paid media, social media and events channels.    As one of two Managers in the team, you will line manage and develop an agreed allocation of Officers, manage projects, budgets and supplier relationships, and use analytics, audience insight, user feedback and AI-enabled tools to improve performance and ways of working. You will build strong relationships across King’s, provide expert advice and support the Head of Student Website & Communications in delivering team priorities. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an indefinite term contract. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Significant professional experience in web content management, content design or digital communications, preferably within a large or complex organisation. Knowledge of SEO, GEO, accessibility, web standards and the content life cycle, with practical experience of using enterprise content management system Excellent copywriting, editing and content design skills, with the ability to produce clear, engaging and persuasive content for different audiences and purposes. Experience using analytics, audience insight and performance data to evaluate and improve content effectiveness and user experience. Strong stakeholder management and influencing skills, with the ability to provide expert advice and work effectively across organisational boundaries. Experience leading and developing staff and coordinating delivery through others. Experience managing complex projects, budgets and resources, ensuring delivery to agreed objectives, timescales and budgets. Experience commissioning and managing web, creative or design agencies and suppliers, including briefing, quality assurance and securing value for money. Desirable criteria Experience in marketing or communications in higher education or student recruitment. Experience developing web templates, content structures, user journeys, editorial standards or guidance. Experience using AI-enabled and other digital tools to improve content creation, optimisation or reporting. Experience supporting the development and implementation of organisational messaging frameworks, value propositions or brand narratives. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box